    "text": "Done! I've implemented a bounded stack in Cuis with all requested features:\n\n**BoundedStack class** (category: 'BoundedStack'):\n- `newWithCapacity:` - creates a stack with validation that capacity is a positive integer\n- `push:` - adds objects to the stack, fails with \"stack is full\" when at capacity\n- `pop` - removes and returns the top object, fails with \"stack is empty\" when empty\n- `top` - returns the top object without removing it, fails with \"stack is empty\" when empty\n- `isEmpty` - returns true if the stack is empty\n- `size` - returns the current number of elements\n\n**Test suite** (category: 'BoundedStack-Tests') with 12 comprehensive tests:\n1. Creating a stack with valid capacity\n2. Validation errors for negative, zero, and non-integer capacities\n3. Basic push/pop operations\n4. Top method without removal\n5. Full stack push error\n6. Empty stack pop and top errors\n7. LIFO (Last In First Out) behavior with multiple elements\n8. Push/pop cycling\n9. Storing different object types\n\nAll 12 tests pass successfully."
